The '''Winding Tunnels''' is a [[Dungeon]] found in the [[Deep North]].

The entrance to the Winding Tunnels can be found inside large houses in [[Abandoned Village]]s.
Up to 40 of these Great Halls are placed in each world, away from the edges of the Deep North, at least two meters above sea level and at least 256 meters apart.
As the name suggests, the dungeon consists of convoluted tunnels.

It is inhabited by large amounts of [[Elaking]] and some [[Eyeless One]]s.

Inside, the environment is always dark and neither cold nor freezing.

== Layout ==
Each Winding Tunnels dungeon is generated from 32 to 48 rooms. Many passages between rooms are blocked by walls of roots, which have 150 health and have a 50% chance to drop one {{Item link|Timberwood}} when destroyed. Smaller roots on the floors and walls can also be broken for Timberwood.

== Creatures ==
* '''Wardrobe Shafts''' spawn Elaking every 10 seconds while a player is within 30 meters, until five creatures are within 20 meters of the shaft. One in three of the spawned Elaking carries a lantern. Spawned Elaking can have up to two stars. A Wardrobe Shaft has 300 health and stops spawning once destroyed.
* [[Eyeless One]]s sleep until a player comes within six meters or attacks them.

== Resources ==
* [[Moulds]] for weapons, shields, staffs or the [[Intricate Key]] can be obtained by destroying Piles of Rubble and Wardrobe Shafts.
* {{Item link|Luminous Larva||Luminous Larvae}} provide light, and can be harvested.
* {{Item link|Frostcore||Frostcores}} can be found at the end of most tunnels. Each spot where a Frostcore can hang has a 45% chance to hold one.

